BabE0s4494S-", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2021-10-31T16:29:43Z", "updated_at": "2021-10-31T16:29:43Z", "body": "MAVSDK uses libcurl to access http. Depending on what is required, we can use different flags/features or libcurl, I believe.\r\n\r\nCan you explain the use case, or why you would require HTTP/2?", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/955745470/reactions", "total_count": 2, "+1": 2, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/959366402", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589#issuecomment-959366402", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589", "id": 959366402, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s45LsUC", "user": {"login": "elpiel", "id": 8925621, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg5MjU2MjE=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8925621?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel", "html_url": "https://github.com/elpiel", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2021-11-03T15:04:45Z", "updated_at": "2021-11-03T15:04:45Z", "body": "When building the mavsdk client from proto files using tonic (https://github.com/hyperium/tonic/) it generates HTTP/2 enabled client.\r\n\r\nThen I saw this article https://grpc.io/blog/grpc-on-http2/ that states:\r\n\r\n> we\u2019ll look at how gRPC builds on HTTP/2\u2019s long-lived connections to create a performant, robust platform for inter-service communication. We will explore the relationship between gRPC and HTTP/2, how gRPC manages HTTP/2 connections, and how gRPC uses HTTP/2 to keep connections alive, healthy, and utilized.\r\n\r\nI was just curious to hear if it's supported and if I can take advantage of the generated HTTP/2 client.\r\n", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/959366402/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/959780094", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589#issuecomment-959780094", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589", "id": 959780094, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s45NRT-", "user": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2021-11-03T17:53:25Z", "updated_at": "2021-11-03T17:53:25Z", "body": "Oh, you're talking about the gRPC side! I don't actually know. I assume we would have to support a secure connection instead of the insecure one?", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/959780094/reactions", "total_count": 1, "+1": 1, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/960316897", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589#issuecomment-960316897", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589", "id": 960316897, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s45PUXh", "user": {"login": "JonasVautherin", "id": 2606672, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDY2NzI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2606672?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin", "html_url": "https://github.com/JonasVautherin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2021-11-04T00:21:38Z", "updated_at": "2021-11-04T00:21:38Z", "body": "I think it does use HTTP/2. What makes you think it doesn't? Does gRPC actually support HTTP/1?", "author_association": "COLLABORATOR", "pin": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/960316897/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "performed_via_github_app": null, "minimized": null}, {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/comments/960556730", "html_url": "https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589#issuecomment-960556730", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/mavlink/MAVSDK/issues/1589", "id": 960556730, "node_id": "IC_kwDOBabE0s45QO66", "user": {"login": "elpiel", "id": 8925621, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg5MjU2MjE=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8925621?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel", "html_url": "https://github.com/elpiel", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/elpiel/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "created_at": "2021-11-04T08:42:05Z", "updated_at": "2021-11-04T08:43:37Z", "body": "> Oh, you're talking about the gRPC side! I don't actually know. I assume we would have to support a secure connection instead of the insecure one?\r\n\r\n@julianoes We can definitely figure out something and here's my suggestion.\r\n\r\nThere's is a Rust crate for end-to-end encryption called Ockam:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/ockam-network/ockam/tree/develop/implementations/rust/ockam/ockam\r\nThere is also a C one: https://github.com/ockam-network/ockam/tree/develop/implementations/c\r\n\r\nI've been looking into building a server-side MAVSDK in Rust.\r\nThe client is automatically built and needs some tweaking, however, using an interceptor on the client for a Rust implemented server-side endpoint could be a PoC for end-to-end encryption.\r\n\r\n> I think it does use HTTP/2. What makes you think it doesn't? Does gRPC actually support HTTP/1?\r\n\r\n@JonasVautherin It does use HTTP/2, you are right. I didn't find anything mentioned in MAVSDK documentation, but I should have checked gRPC documentation too.\r\nFrom my quick search it seems that it does not support 